        "goals": "Keep extending.md's engine/content boundary structural: core (checks/, mount/, engine/, .github/, the top-level docs, and the shared engine modules under packs/ and skills/) must never name a specific pack or skill — packs and skills are discovered content, and a core file citing one couples the engine to its content. One rule per namespace (packs/*, skills/*); reviewed inherent couplings live in each rule's except. migrations/ is deliberately NOT core here: a migration record is a dated one-off that exists to move the fleet off a specific pack's old shape, so naming that pack is its purpose, not a coupling — and the record moves between active_migrations/ and migrations-old/ over its life, which no path-keyed exception can track."
